# Styling conventions

## Source of truth

Global styles flow from `src/app.css`, which imports utilities and component specific styles from `src/lib/styles/*.css`

- **Design tokens** live in `:root` in `app.css` — colors, spacing, container widths, typography scale
- **Component CSS classes** for typography (`.text-*`), surfaces (`.surface-*`), tables (`.table`), and buttons (`.button-*`) live in `src/lib/styles/`
- **Layout utilities** (`.container`, `.text-width`) live in `src/lib/styles/layout.css` (imported from `app.css`)

## Use tokens, not hardcoded values

```css
/* ❌ BAD */
color: #506458;
padding: 16px;

/* ✅ GOOD */
color: var(--muted);
padding: var(--space-medium);
```

Key tokens: `--ink`, `--muted`, `--accent`, `--bg`, `--surface`, `--line`, `--on-accent`, `--on-photo`, `--border-radius`, `--text-width`, container width vars.

## Dark mode

Supported. `mode-watcher` applies `.dark` on `html` (default: system preference). Light values live in `:root`; dark values override the same tokens on `:root.dark`. Components must use tokens, not hardcoded light colors, so both modes stay in sync.

Dark surfaces use the logo hue (`hsl(235 29% 35%)`): `--bg` is `hsl(235 31% 7%)`, `--surface` / `--content-background` lift toward that purple, and `--shadow-*` are purple-black with a faint inner highlight. Header and hero use `--header-bg` / `--hero-bg` (darker purple in dark mode). Photo overlays stay dark chrome (`--on-photo` for icons/text on images). Do not introduce a second visual treatment for the same pattern.

A sun/moon control sits to the right of the EN/SV switch in `SiteHeader`.

## Typography

Allowed variants only — no ad-hoc `font-size` in page scoped CSS:

| Need | Component / class |
|------|-------------------|
| Body text | `<Text variant="body">` (`.text-body`) |
| Page lead | `<Text variant="lead">` or `.lead` |
| Caption / note | `<Text variant="caption">` |
| Label | `<Text variant="label">` |
| Page title | `<Heading as="h1">` (`.page-title`) |
| Section heading | `<Heading as="h2">` (`.page-header`) |
| Sub-section | `<Heading as="h3">` (`.page-sub-section`) |
| Links | `<Link>` (`.link`) |
| Constrained width | `PageContent` (applies `.text-width`) |

Tokens live in `:root` (`--text-*`, `--page-header-*`, `--page-sub-section-*`). Classes in `typography.css`.

Create additional typography classes if needed, but ask first. Page-unique layout leftovers (kontakt map) are intentional; `designguide` keeps its own scoped styles until a future redesign.

## Component-scoped styles

Use `<style>` in `.svelte` files only for layout or structure unique to that component (grid, flex, responsive breakpoints). Pull colors, fonts, and spacing from CSS variables.

```svelte
<style>
	article {
		border-radius: var(--border-radius);
		background: var(--content-background);
		color: var(--muted);
	}
</style>
```

## Images

Use `Image` (`src/lib/components/media/Image.svelte`) for content images. Required: `src`, `alt`, `width`, `height`. Optional: `caption`, `priority` (eager + high fetch priority), `sizes`, `srcset`. Content modules store images as `ContentImage` (`{ src, alt, width, height, srcset? }`). Prefer WebP under `static/mandalon/`; see `README.md` for the add-image procedure.

## Fonts

- Body: Roboto (`body` in `app.css`)
- Headings: Roboto Condensed (`h1–h6` in `app.css`)
- Shared token: `--font-body` (`'Roboto Condensed', 'Roboto', …`) — used by the `Text` component
- Self-hosted in `static/fonts/` — do not add Google Fonts CDN links
- The heading face (Roboto Condensed, latin subset) is preloaded from `SiteChrome` for LCP. Body Roboto loads via CSS.

## Containers & page layout

```html
<PageShell>
  <PageHeader title="…" lead="…" />
  <PageContent>…</PageContent>   <!-- readable line length via .text-width -->
</PageShell>
```

- **Page chrome:** `PageShell` → padding + `.container` (default `--container-width-default`)
- **Body copy:** `PageContent` → `.text-width` (`--text-width`)
- Do not reintroduce `.container-narrow` / `.container-wide` / `--container-width-narrow`; designguide overrides `--container-width` page-locally until redesigned

## CSS delivery

The design system reaches the DOM three ways. Pick the first that fits:

| Mechanism | When to use | Examples |
|-----------|-------------|----------|
| **1. Component emits a global class** | The component *is* the design-system primitive; its root (or known parts) always carry a class defined in `src/lib/styles/` | `Surface` → `.surface` / `.surface-*`; `Text` / `Heading` / `Link` / `Button` → `.text-*`, `.page-title`, `.link`, `.button-*`; `DescriptionList` → `.table` |
| **2. Component applies an existing global class** | A layout helper wraps children and attaches a utility class; it does not redefine the utility | `PageContent` → `.text-width`; `PageShell` → `.container` via its own structure |
| **3. Page (or section) uses a global class in markup** | Shared layout patterns that are not worth a one-line component | `.content-list`, `.surface-grid` on pages |

Do **not** invent a fourth path: a page or component must not declare new **global** selectors (unstyled element names, or classes meant for the whole app) inside a Svelte `<style>` block. Shared look-and-feel belongs in `src/lib/styles/*.css` and is imported from `app.css`.

### `:global()` pierces

Svelte scopes component CSS by default. `:global(...)` is for styling a **child’s** markup that the parent does not own (snippet content, a child component’s root class, or elements rendered by `Image` / `@html`).

**Acceptable** when all of these hold:

1. The selector is rooted under a **local** parent class (e.g. `.media :global(img)`), so the pierce cannot leak site-wide
2. The styles are layout/context for that parent (spacing, object-fit, colour in a hero), not a redefinition of the child’s public API
3. Exposing a prop on the child would be awkward or would force every caller to pass the same layout knobs

**Prefer a prop (or a variant) on the child** instead of `:global()` when the same override repeats, or when the child should own the look (e.g. `Link` `weight` rather than parents restyling `.link`).

**Not acceptable:**

- `:global(body)`, `:global(html)`, or any unscoped element/class that escapes the component
- Pages inventing new global classes in `<style>` for reuse elsewhere — put those in `src/lib/styles/`
- Using `:global()` to avoid moving styles into the component that owns the markup

### Classification of current `:global()` uses

The eleven uses that existed when this rule was written:

| Location | Pierce | Verdict |
|----------|--------|---------|
| `HeroSection` | `.hero-content :global(.page-title)` | Acceptable — local hero layout around `Heading` |
| `HeroSection` | `.hero-copy :global(p)` | Acceptable — colour context for snippet/`Text` children |
| `MediaArticleSection` | `.subtitle :global(p)` | Acceptable — snippet paragraph colour |
| `MediaArticleSection` | `.media :global(figure\|img\|figcaption)` (3) | Acceptable — layout around `Image`; prefer Image props if more variants appear |
| `FeatureCarousel` | `.embla__slide :global(.surface)` | Acceptable — carousel layout of `Surface` |
| `FeatureCarousel` | `.carousel-media :global(img)` | Acceptable — object-fit in fixed aspect box |
| `kontakt/+page` | `.person-details :global(p + p)` | Follow-up — page pierce into `Text`; prefer a stacked snippet wrapper or a prop |

**Also present after T29** (not in the original eleven): `designguide/+page.svelte` pierces many article descendants (`h2`–`h4`, `p`, `li`, `figure`, `img`, gallery classes). **Follow-up** — move those rules into `DesignGuideBody` (which owns the markup) so the page does not style another component’s internals.

## Do not

- Add new global CSS files without importing them from `app.css`
- Introduce CSS frameworks (Tailwind, Bootstrap, etc.)
- Duplicate token values inline in component styles
- Set ad-hoc `font-size` / raw hex colors in page-scoped CSS when a token or typography component exists
- Let pages or components declare new app-wide global selectors in scoped `<style>` blocks
